 "diagnosis": "The outer-loop invariant 'forall i,j :: 0<=i<m && 0<=j<Length1 ==> dst[i,j]==old(src[i,j])' is not maintained. The inner loop modifies dst (the heap), and its invariants say nothing about rows i < m. So after the inner loop Dafny loses the fact that previously copied rows are intact, and cannot re-establish the outer invariant for m+1. Fix: add an inner-loop invariant stating rows 0..m-1 of dst still equal old(src)."}
